text:
Assume `db.query` promisified (e.g. `mysql2/promise` or `util.promisify`):

```javascript
async function getUser(id) {
  const [rows] = await db.query('SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ?', [id]);
  if (!rows.length) throw new Error('Not found');
  return rows[0];
}
```

Call site:

```javascript
// try/catch replaces err callback
try {
  const user = await getUser(42);
} catch (err) {
  console.error(err);
}
```

---

**If `db.query` not yet promisified:**

```javascript
const { promisify } = require('util');
const query = promisify(db.query).bind(db);

async function getUser(id) {
  const rows = await query('SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ?', [id]);
  if (!rows.length) throw new Error('Not found');
  return rows[0];
}
```

---

Key changes:

| Before | After |
|--------|-------|
| `callback(err)` | `throw err` |
| `callback(null, val)` | `return val` |
| Nested fn | Flat `await` |
| Caller checks `err` arg | Caller uses `try/catch` |
